# Wallet module — Phase 0 architecture contract

**Phase:** 0 (foundational preparation)  
**Runtime status:** Pure `packages/wallet-core` domain + tenant-scoped Prisma persistence (Phase 2C). No HTTP routes or product UI implemented.
**Authority:** [ADR-WALLET-001](./adr/ADR-WALLET-001-member-wallet-bounded-context.mdoc)

---

## 1. Existing “wallet” name collision impact report

### 1.1 Registration finance / synthetic ledger (not Member Wallet)

| Symbol / pattern | Location | Meaning | Member Wallet conflict |
| ---------------- | -------- | ------- | ---------------------- |
| `bookingWalletId(registrationId)` | `packages/workspaces/denali/src/finance/ledger-accounts.ts` | GL credit account `booking:{registrationId}` | **High** — name implies member wallet; actually registration sub-ledger |
| `financeWs2BookingWalletId` … `financeWs6BookingWalletId` | `packages/workspaces/finance-ws*/src/finance/chart-of-accounts.ts` | Prefixed `wsN:booking:{registrationId}` accounts | **High** — same semantics, certification workspaces |
| `LEDGER_ACCOUNTS` / `FINANCE_WS*_LEDGER_ACCOUNTS` | Denali + finance-ws chart-of-accounts | Operator clearing, discount contra GL codes | **Low** — no “wallet” in export name except comments |
| `walletNetMinor` | `packages/finance-core/src/domain/compile-invoice-balances.ts`, web finance/tour UI | Invoice field: prepayment + paid − refunds for one registration | **High** — reads like member balance; is derived read model only |
| `finance.ledger.capture`, `finance.ledger.double_entry_applied` | Outbox / `prisma-finance.repository.ts` | Registration payment journal events | **Medium** — “ledger” overlap; different aggregate |
| ADR-010 “booking wallet credit” | `docs/phase-20/p7/appendices/adr/ADR-010-*.md` | XOR between TourCreated and payment capture on registration account | **Medium** — terminology only; finance scoped |

**Phase 0 action:** Document only. No renames (production strings, tests, and finance golden guards depend on current names).

### 1.2 Member portal stub (placeholder for future Member Wallet)

| Symbol / pattern | Location | Meaning | Member Wallet conflict |
| ---------------- | -------- | ------- | ---------------------- |
| `member.module.wallet` | `evaluate-member-portal-entitlements.ts`, API entitlements | Entitlement key for portal module id `wallet` | **None** — correct future surface |
| `/me/wallet` | `guest-full-v1` preset, generated portal surfaces | Route path for hidden module | **None** |
| `MemberModuleStub` + `walletLede` | `apps/portal/src/me/member-module-stub.tsx` | Placeholder copy when no workspace renderer | **Low** — replace with workspace renderer in Phase 3 |
| `portalModuleGrants: ["wallet"]` | `PortalMemberPlan`, membership metadata | Tenant opt-in for hidden module | **None** — enablement model |

### 1.3 Module gates (finance reference — not wallet yet)

| Mechanism | Location | Purpose |
| --------- | -------- | ------- |
| `workspaceFinance.supported` | `workspace.manifest.json` | Product declares finance capability |
| `isFinanceModuleEnabled(theme, workspaceType)` | `apps/api/.../finance-module-enabled.ts` | Theme `enabledModules` + default-when-unset |
| `assertFinanceWorkspaceGate` / `FORBIDDEN_FINANCE_MODULE_DISABLED` | `assert-finance-access.ts` | API fail-closed gate |
| `capabilities.financeNav` | workspace plugin + `apps/web` finance-nav-registry | Operator UI visibility |

Wallet will mirror this pattern under `workspaceWallet` (Section 3).

---

## 2. `workspaceWallet` manifest contract (Phase 1 foundation)

Normative shape implemented in Phase 1 (`WorkspaceWalletBlockSchema` + codegen). **No production workspace manifest declares `workspaceWallet` yet** — bindings remain empty until a workspace opts in.

```typescript
/** Documentation contract — not shipped TypeScript */
type WorkspaceWalletBlock = {
  /** Product declares wallet support for this workspace package. */
  readonly supported: boolean;
  /** When theme.enabledModules is empty/unset, default enable if true (finance pattern). */
  readonly defaultModuleEnabledWhenUnset?: boolean;
  readonly capabilities: {
    /** Member stored-value accounts + ledger. */
    readonly memberAccounts: boolean;
    /** Operator reconciliation / adjustments UI. */
    readonly ops: boolean;
    /** Top-up via gateway PSP (optional Phase 2+; requires commerce.paymentMode gateway — not Phase 0/1) */
    readonly gatewayTopUp?: boolean;
    /** Withdrawal / payout workflow (optional). */
    readonly withdrawals?: boolean;
  };
  /** Workspace-owned ledger policy (account naming, limits) — module + export binding. */
  readonly ledgerPolicy?: { readonly module: string; readonly export: string };
  /** Workspace-owned operator limits / KYC policy adapter. */
  readonly operatorPolicy?: { readonly module: string; readonly export: string };
  /** Operator ops panel manifest (theme-aware), mirror workspaceFinance.opsManifest. */
  readonly opsManifest?: {
    readonly module: string;
    readonly defaultExport: string;
    readonly resolveFromThemeExport?: string;
  };
};
```

### 2.1 Enablement semantics (mirror finance)

| Input | Expected behavior |
| ----- | ----------------- |
| `theme.enabledModules` contains `"wallet"` | Module enabled |
| `enabledModules` non-empty and omits `"wallet"` | Module disabled → `FORBIDDEN_WALLET_MODULE_DISABLED` |
| `enabledModules` empty/unset | Use `defaultModuleEnabledWhenUnset` from codegen binding |
| `workspaceWallet.supported !== true` | `WALLET_WORKSPACE_UNSUPPORTED` |

Theme key name **`wallet`** is reserved for module enablement (parallel to `"finance"`).

### 2.2 Member portal integration

| Concern | Contract |
| ------- | -------- |
| Module id | `wallet` (existing preset `guest-full-v1`) |
| Entitlement key | `member.module.wallet` |
| Default tier | `hidden` — requires `portalModuleGrants` or plan `moduleGrants` |
| Renderer | `plugin.capabilities.memberPortalRenderers.renderers.wallet` via `registerWorkspaceMemberPortalRenderers` |
| Route gate | Portal dispatcher + `isMemberModuleEntitled` (unchanged) |
| Capability flags | `member.module.wallet.{read,export,...}` via `PortalMemberPlan.capabilityFlags` |

### 2.3 Workspace-specific adapters (never in platform core)

- Ledger account prefix / naming policy
- Per-tenant currency default (from `commerce.currency` or wallet-specific override)
- Operator adjustment reason codes
- Optional integration with registration finance (event subscription only)

